   "id": "root",
   "x": 505,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Vision loss in ONE eye: the problem is in FRONT of the optic chiasm",
   "lines": [
    "ask: pain? sudden or gradual? all or part of the field? baseline acuity? diabetes, hypertension, eye history",
    "examine: acuity · confrontation fields · swinging flashlight (RAPD = retina or optic nerve) · red reflex · pressure",
    "PAINFUL: cornea, uveitis, acute angle closure (see the RED EYE chart)"
   ]
  },
  {
